  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1115 AM CDT Sat Jun 27 2026\n\nWe've been quite lucky here in Middle Tennessee so far this \nsummer with a reasonable and should I say almost pleasant summer \nas far as temperatures. Well, that luck runs out beginning Sunday\nwith things cranking up a few more notches by Monday. \n\nSince this is the first significant heat wave of the summer, we \nreally wanted to get the message out early that extreme heat and \nhigh humidity will set up camp over the area through at least \nFriday. And since this might be the most outdoorsy week/weekend \ncoming up with the holiday, we wanted to make sure everyone plans \naccordingly for any outdoor events scheduled. \n\nMost of Middle Tennessee especially west of the Cumberland \nPlateau will be impacted with afternoon heat index readings \nbetween 105F-109F degrees with some locations topping over 110+F.\nAnd to put salt into our wounds even more, low temperatures will \nunfortunately just not get that low with these same locations \nexperiencing lows in the mid to upper 70s which won't allow much \nfor overnight cooling recovery. \n\nConfidence is very high for heat impacts on Monday and Tuesday. As\nwe get to mid and end of the week, some lucky locations could see\nan small increase in chances for afternoon and evening pop-up\nthunderstorms. Obviously, any pop-up thunderstorms that can \ndevelop would be a welcome short-term relief to the heat, but \ntruly don't think widespread storms will develop to significantly \nimpact our heat wave. But at this point after looking at these\ntemperatures, I'm holding on to the chance. \n\nRegardless, brace yourselves for the heat, humidity, and a slew \nof Heat Advisories and possibly even Extreme Heat Warnings for \nthis upcoming work week/holiday weekend.",
